        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Complete author Theorem3.1 proof and full new independence core Proposition3.2, decay estimate3.3 and phase-sign lemma3.4 are supplied. Gamma is a discontinuous group acting properly discontinuously and freely on AdS3, and condition2.9 requires constants A,a with N_Gamma(x,R)<A exp(aR) uniformly for every x and R>0. The conclusion is lim_m dim_C L2_(lambda_m)(Gamma backslash AdS3)=infinity, where lambda_m=4m(m-1) as fixed in the source. The proof first conjugates Gamma to obtain positive separation via the written Baire argument2.7/2.9 and then gives the explicit threshold m_Gamma(k) and coefficient-tail comparison. Prior existence/L2 convergence of the generalized Poincare series is genuinely established Kassel–Kobayashi background identified in Fact2.4. This is the general exponential-growth statement, not an assertion of infinite multiplicity at each finite m, and it does not assert an elliptic Weyl law. Stable-deformation and orbifold variants are not separately counted."
      },
